1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,215
You work hard. You get paid.

2
00:00:02,115 --> 00:00:04,543
And yet, somehow, there's never enough left

3
00:00:04,443 --> 00:00:05,842
at the end of the month.

4
00:00:06,122 --> 00:00:07,144
Most of the time,

5
00:00:07,044 --> 00:00:08,935
it's not about how much you earn.

6
00:00:09,215 --> 00:00:11,187
It's about a few quiet habits that

7
00:00:11,087 --> 00:00:13,554
drain your money without you even noticing.

8
00:00:13,834 --> 00:00:16,216
Today, we're going through seven of them,

9
00:00:16,116 --> 00:00:17,942
and exactly what to do instead.

10
00:00:18,742 --> 00:00:21,782
Habit number one is saving whatever is left over.

11
00:00:22,062 --> 00:00:25,049
The problem? There's almost never anything left over.

12
00:00:25,329 --> 00:00:27,276
Flip the order. The day you get

13
00:00:27,176 --> 00:00:29,957
paid, move a fixed amount into savings first.

14
00:00:30,237 --> 00:00:32,384
Even ten percent is a great start.

15
00:00:32,284 --> 00:00:34,009
Work your way up to twenty.

16
00:00:34,809 --> 00:00:37,011
Habit number two is impulse shopping.

17
00:00:37,291 --> 00:00:38,948
A quick scroll, a flash sale,

18
00:00:38,848 --> 00:00:40,290
one click, and it's done.

19
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:42,313
Try the forty eight hour rule.

20
00:00:42,213 --> 00:00:44,777
When you want something that isn't essential,

21
00:00:44,677 --> 00:00:46,858
add it to your cart and wait two days.

22
00:00:47,138 --> 00:00:49,000
If you still want it after forty

23
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,873
eight hours, buy it without guilt.

24
00:00:50,773 --> 00:00:52,415
Most of the time, you won't.

25
00:00:53,215 --> 00:00:55,821
Habit number three is called lifestyle creep.

26
00:00:56,101 --> 00:00:56,994
You get a raise,

27
00:00:56,894 --> 00:00:59,175
and your spending rises right along with it.

28
00:00:59,455 --> 00:01:01,726
A nicer apartment, a new car payment,

29
00:01:01,626 --> 00:01:02,724
more dinners out.

30
00:01:03,004 --> 00:01:04,945
Instead, when your income goes up,

31
00:01:04,845 --> 00:01:07,166
keep your lifestyle the same for a while.

32
00:01:07,446 --> 00:01:09,188
Send at least half of every raise

33
00:01:09,088 --> 00:01:11,179
straight to your savings and your goals.

34
00:01:11,979 --> 00:01:14,599
Habit number four is not having a budget.

35
00:01:14,879 --> 00:01:17,293
Without a plan, your spending quietly becomes

36
00:01:17,193 --> 00:01:18,527
bigger than your income.

37
00:01:18,807 --> 00:01:20,704
A budget isn't about restriction.

38
00:01:20,604 --> 00:01:22,773
It's about telling your money where to

39
00:01:22,673 --> 00:01:24,896
go, instead of wondering where it went.

40
00:01:25,176 --> 00:01:27,339
Start simple. Write down your income,

41
00:01:27,239 --> 00:01:29,791
your bills, and a limit for everything else.

42
00:01:30,591 --> 00:01:33,174
Habit number five is using credit cards

43
00:01:33,074 --> 00:01:34,320
like extra income.

44
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:37,254
High interest turns a small purchase into

45
00:01:37,154 --> 00:01:38,625
a big, long term cost.

46
00:01:38,905 --> 00:01:40,750
Use cards only for what you can

47
00:01:40,650 --> 00:01:42,269
pay off in full each month.

48
00:01:42,549 --> 00:01:44,647
And if you already carry a balance,

49
00:01:44,547 --> 00:01:46,417
list your debts and pay off the

50
00:01:46,317 --> 00:01:48,814
smallest one first, then roll that payment

51
00:01:48,714 --> 00:01:49,614
into the next.

52
00:01:50,414 --> 00:01:53,495
Habit number six is thinking small amounts don't matter.

53
00:01:53,775 --> 00:01:55,804
Five dollars a day is over eighteen

54
00:01:55,704 --> 00:01:57,071
hundred dollars a year.

55
00:01:57,351 --> 00:01:58,790
Try a simple challenge.

56
00:01:58,690 --> 00:02:00,478
Pick a few no spend days each

57
00:02:00,378 --> 00:02:02,515
week, and track them on a calendar.

58
00:02:02,795 --> 00:02:05,081
Watching those little wins stack up is

59
00:02:04,981 --> 00:02:07,152
one of the best motivators there is.

60
00:02:07,952 --> 00:02:10,149
And habit number seven is waiting for

61
00:02:10,049 --> 00:02:11,623
the perfect time to start.

62
00:02:11,903 --> 00:02:13,540
Someday, when I earn more.

63
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,372
Someday, when things calm down.

64
00:02:15,652 --> 00:02:17,731
But time is the most powerful tool

65
00:02:17,631 --> 00:02:19,885
your money has. The sooner you start,

66
00:02:19,785 --> 00:02:21,108
the more it can grow.

67
00:02:21,388 --> 00:02:23,576
So open that savings account today.

68
00:02:23,476 --> 00:02:25,247
Write your budget this week.

69
00:02:25,147 --> 00:02:27,454
And automate your savings this month.

70
00:02:28,254 --> 00:02:29,612
Let's do a quick recap.

71
00:02:29,892 --> 00:02:32,861
Save first, and wait forty eight hours before buying.

72
00:02:33,141 --> 00:02:35,367
Keep your lifestyle steady when you earn

73
00:02:35,267 --> 00:02:37,226
more, and give every dollar a plan.

74
00:02:37,506 --> 00:02:38,918
Pay your cards in full,

75
00:02:38,818 --> 00:02:40,571
and celebrate the small wins.

76
00:02:40,851 --> 00:02:43,548
And most importantly, start today, not someday.

77
00:02:44,348 --> 00:02:46,116
You don't need to fix all seven

78
00:02:46,016 --> 00:02:48,430
at once. Pick just one and start this week.

79
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:50,213
If this video helped you,

80
00:02:50,113 --> 00:02:52,289
like it and subscribe for more simple

81
00:02:52,189 --> 00:02:54,759
ways to build a better life with your money.

82
00:02:55,039 --> 00:02:56,836
Tell me in the comments which habit

83
00:02:56,736 --> 00:02:59,116
you're breaking first. See you in the next one.
